      <p>For <strong>7.25 years at Sony Semiconductor Manufacturing</strong>, I built manufacturing execution systems (MES) and an AI scheduling system for fab operations — work that received a <strong>Department Manager Award (AI/DX)</strong>. Today I am a <strong>Senior Consultant at BayCurrent Consulting</strong>, where my client work includes a POS system built in C# around finite-state-machine design.</p>
      <p>My working rule is simple: <strong>AI earns its place by measurement, not by demo.</strong> Every AI component I ship is benchmarked against a rule-based baseline on the same data. Where it wins, it stays. Where it loses, it moves to explaining — and the losses are published too.</p>
      <p>That discipline produced my flagship project below.</p>
