    <section id="flagship">
      <div class="sec-head"><span class="num">02.</span><h2>Flagship — ResiliMES-AI</h2></div>
      <p class="lede">Right-click a bar — or an idle gap — on a fab Gantt chart and ask “why?”.</p>
      <p>A fab schedule spans <strong>1,313 tools, 2,156 lots and 264 Q-time constraints</strong>. Nobody can read it end to end, so floor leads override it from experience — most often by filling an idle gap that was, in fact, protecting a downstream Q-time window. ResiliMES-AI puts the answer on the chart itself: a rule kernel makes every decision and records its reasons; the AI only explains, and every number in its answer is fact-checked by code. Built for the Open Agent Hackathon 2026, Track 02 — “The Agent That Can Explain Why”.</p>
      <figure class="flagship-card">
        <div class="shot">
          <div class="step">1 — Right-click a bar or gap</div>
          <img src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Toygaolingxiao/ResiliMES-AI/main/docs/deck/img/p5_menu.jpg" alt="ResiliMES-AI Gantt chart with right-click investigation menu">
          <figcaption>The investigation entry: right-click any bar, gap, or the time axis on the Gantt.</figcaption>
        </div>
        <div class="shot">
          <div class="step">2 — The explanation panel, every number fact-checked</div>
          <img src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Toygaolingxiao/ResiliMES-AI/main/docs/deck/img/p5_panel.jpg" alt="ResiliMES-AI investigation panel with the fact-checked explanation">
          <figcaption>The answer comes from the scheduler's own decision record. The AI drafts the explanation; code checks every number before it is shown.</figcaption>
        </div>
        <table>
          <tr><th>Test</th><th>Measured result</th></tr>
          <tr><td>Fill the gaps</td><td>Filling all 6,864 deliberate idle gaps in a 48 h run raises avoidable Q-time violations from <b>23 → 42</b>. The gaps are decisions, not waste.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Shift-note extraction</td><td>AI-extracted shift notes cut avoidable Q-time violations <b>17 → 14</b> — matching the gold-standard events, with <b>0 new violations</b>.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Remove the AI</td><td>Removing Nemotron leaves the schedule <b>unchanged</b>: 0 AI calls in the default run. The AI never writes the schedule.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>AI duty officer</td><td>Under factory trigger settings, the AI escalation path fired <b>0 times</b> — the rule kernel handled every anomaly. Reported as measured, not dressed up as a feature.</td></tr>
        </table>
        <div class="links-row">
          <a href="https://github.com/Toygaolingxiao/ResiliMES-AI">GitHub repository ↗</a>
          <span class="placeholder" id="demo-video-placeholder">Demo video — link to be added</span>
        </div>
      </figure>
